---
interface Props {
  lang?: 'es' | 'en';
}

const { lang = 'en' } = Astro.props;

const content = {
  en: {
    eyebrow: 'Projects',
    title: 'A legal-tech platform: backend, data, and infrastructure',
    description:
      'Arxatec is a Peruvian legal platform built as several independent services that talk to each other through explicit contracts. My scope is the backend, the legal data pipeline, and the infrastructure underneath — the web clients are outside it.',
    featured: {
      name: 'Arxatec',
      kind: 'Legal-tech platform · Peru',
      scope: 'Scope: backend, data, and infrastructure',
      note: 'Private repositories',
      summary:
        'A corpus of public legal documents plus an AI assistant for lawyers. A scraper feeds the corpus, a Python microservice indexes it and answers RAG queries over it, and a Node API carries the product itself: cases, calendar, documents, chat, and billing.',
      stack: [
        'Node.js',
        'TypeScript',
        'Express 5',
        'Prisma 7',
        'PostgreSQL',
        'Redis',
        'BullMQ',
        'Socket.IO',
        'Python',
        'FastAPI',
        'Qdrant',
        'LangChain',
        'AWS S3',
        'Docker',
        'Nginx',
      ],
      bullets: [
        'Vertical Slice Architecture: every endpoint is a self-contained unit owning its domain, data, and presentation layers — 16 modules and over 400 HTTP slices in the main API.',
        'Cross-repo contracts that cannot be changed in a single repo: the canonical source catalog has its SHA-256 fingerprint pinned in the test suites of three repositories at once.',
        'Migrated the assistant chat from Python to Node while keeping the SSE contract the client already consumed frozen.',
        'Credit-based billing across two payment providers (MercadoPago and Polar), per-model token accounting, and metering of AI usage.',
        'VPS deployment with Docker, Nginx, and pm2 — including diagnosing failures that only surface in production, such as the ESM/CJS crash-loop of the Prisma 7 client on Node 22.',
      ],
    },
    componentsTitle: 'The services',
    components: [
      {
        name: 'arxatec-lawyer-service',
        kind: 'Product API · Node.js',
        summary:
          'Express 5 API in strict TypeScript over PostgreSQL with Prisma. Cases, contacts, calendar, documents, kanban, chat, finances, notifications, and billing.',
        bullets: [
          '16 modules, 400+ HTTP slices, and roughly 6,800 unit tests',
          'Background work with BullMQ and Redis; real time over Socket.IO and SSE',
          'PDF/DOCX generation, OCR, and S3 storage',
          'Seven CI gates: lint, types, test types, dependency boundaries, tests, and build',
        ],
        tech: ['Express 5', 'Prisma 7', 'PostgreSQL', 'Redis', 'BullMQ', 'Socket.IO', 'Zod', 'Jest'],
      },
      {
        name: 'arxatec-lawyer-assistant',
        kind: 'RAG microservice · Python',
        summary:
          'FastAPI service that ingests documents from S3, splits them, generates embeddings, and indexes them in Qdrant to answer with verifiable legal context.',
        bullets: [
          'Ingestion pipeline: extraction → chunking → embeddings → Qdrant + PostgreSQL',
          'Every answer traceable back to the document and its official source',
          'Ingestion bottleneck measured rather than assumed: the cost was not Qdrant (0.4% of the time) but one embedding request per chunk, issued serially',
          'Schema migrations with Alembic and SQLAlchemy',
        ],
        tech: ['FastAPI', 'LangChain', 'Qdrant', 'SQLAlchemy', 'Alembic', 'AWS S3', 'Poetry'],
      },
      {
        name: 'arxatec-scrapping',
        kind: 'Legal data pipeline · TypeScript',
        summary:
          'Scraper for Peru’s public legal sources: 33 sources covered by 21 modules, all producing the same ingestion contract.',
        bullets: [
          'Resumable by design: ledger plus checkpoint per source, so a retry never duplicates',
          'Per-source anti-blocking (throttling, headers, residential IP), documented case by case',
          'OCR fallback for scanned PDFs the backend rejects',
          'A single smoke command returns a PASS/FAIL verdict before a module is called done',
        ],
        tech: ['TypeScript', 'Puppeteer', 'Cheerio', 'Tesseract OCR', 'Qdrant', 'PostgreSQL', 'AWS S3'],
      },
    ],
    practiceTitle: 'How it stays maintainable',
    practiceDescription:
      'The platform is large enough that memory does not scale. What keeps it workable is a habit: never assume documentation is current — check it against the code before relying on it, and fix what drifted in the same change.',
    practiceItems: [
      'Dated session record: every audit or decision lands in a folder for that day, declaring the commit it was verified against.',
      'The reasoning lives in each unit’s README rather than scattered comments — over 570 of them across modules, features, and slices.',
      'Mechanical verification before anything is called done: lint, types, tests, and build. Nothing closes on visual inspection.',
      'A branch and a pull request per unit of work; never a direct push to main.',
    ],
  },
  es: {
    eyebrow: 'Proyectos',
    title: 'Una plataforma legal-tech: backend, datos e infraestructura',
    description:
      'Arxatec es una plataforma legal peruana construida como varios servicios independientes que se comunican mediante contratos explícitos. Mi alcance es el backend, el pipeline de datos legales y la infraestructura que los sostiene — los clientes web quedan fuera.',
    featured: {
      name: 'Arxatec',
      kind: 'Plataforma legal-tech · Perú',
      scope: 'Alcance: backend, datos e infraestructura',
      note: 'Repositorios privados',
      summary:
        'Un corpus de documentos legales públicos y un asistente con IA para abogados. Un scraper alimenta el corpus, un microservicio Python lo indexa y responde consultas RAG sobre él, y una API Node sostiene el producto: casos, agenda, documentos, chat y cobros.',
      stack: [
        'Node.js',
        'TypeScript',
        'Express 5',
        'Prisma 7',
        'PostgreSQL',
        'Redis',
        'BullMQ',
        'Socket.IO',
        'Python',
        'FastAPI',
        'Qdrant',
        'LangChain',
        'AWS S3',
        'Docker',
        'Nginx',
      ],
      bullets: [
        'Arquitectura Vertical Slice: cada endpoint es una unidad autónoma con sus capas de dominio, datos y presentación — 16 módulos y más de 400 slices HTTP en la API principal.',
        'Contratos entre repositorios que no se pueden cambiar en uno solo: el catálogo de fuentes canónicas lleva su huella SHA-256 fijada en los tests de tres repositorios a la vez.',
        'Migración del chat del asistente de Python a Node manteniendo congelado el contrato SSE que el cliente ya consumía.',
        'Cobro por créditos con dos pasarelas (MercadoPago y Polar), contabilidad de tokens por modelo y medición del consumo de IA.',
        'Despliegue en VPS con Docker, Nginx y pm2, incluyendo el diagnóstico de fallos que solo aparecen en producción — como el crash-loop ESM/CJS del cliente de Prisma 7 sobre Node 22.',
      ],
    },
    componentsTitle: 'Los servicios',
    components: [
      {
        name: 'arxatec-lawyer-service',
        kind: 'API de producto · Node.js',
        summary:
          'API Express 5 en TypeScript estricto sobre PostgreSQL con Prisma. Casos, contactos, agenda, documentos, kanban, chat, finanzas, notificaciones y facturación.',
        bullets: [
          '16 módulos, más de 400 slices HTTP y alrededor de 6.800 tests unitarios',
          'Trabajo asíncrono con BullMQ y Redis; tiempo real con Socket.IO y SSE',
          'Generación de PDF/DOCX, OCR y almacenamiento en S3',
          'Siete gates de CI: lint, tipos, tipos de tests, límites de dependencias, tests y build',
        ],
        tech: ['Express 5', 'Prisma 7', 'PostgreSQL', 'Redis', 'BullMQ', 'Socket.IO', 'Zod', 'Jest'],
      },
      {
        name: 'arxatec-lawyer-assistant',
        kind: 'Microservicio RAG · Python',
        summary:
          'Servicio FastAPI que ingiere documentos desde S3, los trocea, genera embeddings y los indexa en Qdrant para responder con contexto legal verificable.',
        bullets: [
          'Pipeline de ingesta: extracción → troceado → embeddings → Qdrant + PostgreSQL',
          'Cada respuesta es trazable hasta el documento y su fuente oficial',
          'Cuello de botella de la ingesta medido, no supuesto: el coste no estaba en Qdrant (0,4 % del tiempo) sino en un embedding por chunk lanzado en serie',
          'Migraciones de esquema con Alembic y SQLAlchemy',
        ],
        tech: ['FastAPI', 'LangChain', 'Qdrant', 'SQLAlchemy', 'Alembic', 'AWS S3', 'Poetry'],
      },
      {
        name: 'arxatec-scrapping',
        kind: 'Pipeline de datos legales · TypeScript',
        summary:
          'Scraper de las fuentes legales públicas del Perú: 33 fuentes cubiertas por 21 módulos, todos armando el mismo contrato de ingesta.',
        bullets: [
          'Reanudable por diseño: ledger y checkpoint por fuente, así un reintento nunca duplica',
          'Anti-bloqueo por fuente (throttling, cabeceras, IP residencial), documentado caso a caso',
          'OCR de respaldo para los PDF escaneados que el backend rechaza',
          'Un solo comando de smoke devuelve veredicto PASS/FAIL antes de dar un módulo por bueno',
        ],
        tech: ['TypeScript', 'Puppeteer', 'Cheerio', 'Tesseract OCR', 'Qdrant', 'PostgreSQL', 'AWS S3'],
      },
    ],
    practiceTitle: 'Cómo se mantiene mantenible',
    practiceDescription:
      'La plataforma es lo bastante grande como para que la memoria no escale. Lo que la sostiene es una costumbre: nunca dar por actualizada la documentación — comprobarla contra el código antes de apoyarse en ella y corregir lo desfasado en el mismo cambio.',
    practiceItems: [
      'Registro de sesión fechado: cada auditoría o decisión queda en la carpeta de ese día, declarando el commit contra el que se verificó.',
      'El porqué vive en el README de cada unidad de código, no en comentarios sueltos: más de 570 entre módulos, features y slices.',
      'Verificación mecánica antes de dar algo por bueno: lint, tipos, tests y build. Nada se cierra por inspección visual.',
      'Una rama y un pull request por unidad de trabajo; nunca un push directo a main.',
    ],
  },
};

const t = content[lang];
---

<section class="space-y-12">
  <div class="max-w-3xl space-y-4">
    <p class="text-sm font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-neutral-500 dark:text-neutral-400">
      {t.eyebrow}
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-neutral-950 dark:text-white md:text-4xl">
      {t.title}
    </h2>

    <p class="text-base leading-8 text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-300 md:text-lg">
      {t.description}
    </p>
  </div>

  <article class="rounded-3xl border border-neutral-200 bg-white/80 p-7 shadow-sm transition duration-300 hover:-translate-y-1 hover:border-neutral-300 hover:shadow-lg dark:border-white/10 dark:bg-white/5 dark:hover:border-white/15 dark:hover:bg-white/[0.07]">
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-4 md:flex-row md:items-start md:justify-between">
      <div>
        <h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-neutral-950 dark:text-white">
          {t.featured.name}
        </h3>

        <p class="mt-1 text-sm font-medium text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-200">
          {t.featured.kind}
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="text-sm text-neutral-500 dark:text-neutral-400 md:text-right">
        <p>{t.featured.scope}</p>
        <p>{t.featured.note}</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="mt-5 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-7 text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-300 md:text-base">
      {t.featured.summary}
    </p>

    <div class="mt-5 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
      {t.featured.stack.map((tech) => (
        <span class="rounded-full border border-neutral-200 bg-neutral-50 px-3 py-1 text-xs text-neutral-700 transition hover:border-green-500/40 hover:text-neutral-950 dark:border-white/10 dark:bg-white/[0.04] dark:text-neutral-300 dark:hover:border-green-500/40 dark:hover:text-white">
          {tech}
        </span>
      ))}
    </div>

    <ul class="mt-6 space-y-3 text-sm leading-7 text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-300">
      {t.featured.bullets.map((bullet) => (
        <li class="group flex gap-3">
          <span class="mt-2 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-neutral-400 transition group-hover:bg-green-500 dark:bg-neutral-500"></span>
          <span>{bullet}</span>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
  </article>

  <div class="space-y-5">
    <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-neutral-950 dark:text-white">
      {t.componentsTitle}
    </h3>

    <div class="grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-3">
      {t.components.map((project) => (
        <article class="group flex flex-col rounded-3xl border border-neutral-200 bg-white/80 p-6 shadow-sm transition duration-300 hover:-translate-y-1 hover:border-neutral-300 hover:shadow-lg dark:border-white/10 dark:bg-white/5 dark:hover:border-white/15 dark:hover:bg-white/[0.07]">
          <h4 class="break-words font-mono text-base font-semibold text-neutral-950 dark:text-white">
            {project.name}
          </h4>

          <p class="mt-1 text-sm font-medium text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-200">
            {project.kind}
          </p>

          <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-7 text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-300">
            {project.summary}
          </p>

          <ul class="mt-5 space-y-3 text-sm leading-7 text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-300">
            {project.bullets.map((bullet) => (
              <li class="flex gap-3">
                <span class="mt-2 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-neutral-400 transition group-hover:bg-green-500 dark:bg-neutral-500"></span>
                <span>{bullet}</span>
              </li>
            ))}
          </ul>

          <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-2 pt-1">
            {project.tech.map((tech) => (
              <span class="rounded-full border border-neutral-200 bg-neutral-50 px-3 py-1 text-xs text-neutral-700 transition hover:border-green-500/40 hover:text-neutral-950 dark:border-white/10 dark:bg-white/[0.04] dark:text-neutral-300 dark:hover:border-green-500/40 dark:hover:text-white">
                {tech}
              </span>
            ))}
          </div>
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>

  <article class="group rounded-3xl border border-neutral-200 bg-white/80 p-6 shadow-sm dark:border-white/10 dark:bg-white/5">
    <div class="max-w-3xl space-y-3">
      <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-neutral-950 dark:text-white">
        {t.practiceTitle}
      </h3>

      <p class="text-sm leading-7 text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-300">
        {t.practiceDescription}
      </p>
    </div>

    <ul class="mt-5 grid gap-3 md:grid-cols-2">
      {t.practiceItems.map((item) => (
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3 text-sm leading-7 text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-300">
          <span class="mt-2 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-neutral-400 transition group-hover:bg-green-500 dark:bg-neutral-500"></span>
          <span>{item}</span>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
  </article>
</section>
